B.kG=new A.a3(B.ET,["Aechak Plush","Your attachment style,\nas a little plush","16 plushies + 1 secret \xb7 16 questions \xb7 3 minutes","Drop a coin and start","Continue your test","Look who's waiting for you","Different little hearts, all worth loving.","What is an attachment style?","It's your way of connecting with someone close. Meet the two sides of attachment\u2014anxiety and avoidance\u2014as a little plush.","Not a diagnosis","How long does it take?","Just answer 16 everyday situations. Your plush is about 3 minutes away!","Can my result change?","Yes. Attachment can change with relationship experiences. You may also be different in love and in friendship.","How do I check compatibility?","Send a red-thread invitation from your result. We'll connect two plushies drawn in the same mode.","What about my privacy?","No login. Your records stay on this device. Shared links contain scores, mode, scoring version and your optional nickname.","Who are you\nthinking of?","Choose one person who comes to mind.","Love mode","Partner, someone you're seeing or a crush","Friendship mode","Your best friend or closest friend","Name on your plush tag (optional)","For example: Fluffy","{name}'s attachment plush","Please use up to 8 characters.","Please choose a kinder nickname.","Let's draw!","Choose a mode first","Previous question","Continue later","Test progress","The plushies are waiting with fluttering hearts\u2026","Halfway! The claw is getting ready","Almost there. Four coins left!","Measuring the anxiety gauge\u2026","Pulling the avoidance lever\u2026","Adding fluffy stuffing\u2026","Tying the ribbon\u2026","Checking for a secret plush\u2026","Skip","Got one!","\u2026Wait, could this be?","Meet my plush","Save it now","Tap your plush to hear its little thoughts","This is the plush {name} drew","Me","A friend","My attachment plush","This is my kind of plush","Attachment map","Anxiety","Avoidance","Low","High","How much you worry about losing a relationship","How uncomfortable closeness and relying on others feel","Materials: anxiety {a}% \xb7 avoidance {v}% \xb7 fluff 100%","Handle-with-care label","Made in my heart","What makes you lovable","When your heart wobbles","A little heart-mending tip","A lovely match","Handle with extra care","Estimated appearance rate {rate}%","Appearance rates are simulated estimates from the PRD, not measured user statistics.","Draw again in the other mode","Draw my own plush","Plush collection","My plush collection","{count} of 17 collected","{count} rare","Shelf view","Map view","Find a friend who has this plush","Finish a test or check compatibility with a friend to fill your collection.","A friend's plush met through compatibility","Mine","Friend's","A red thread has arrived","{name} sent you a red thread","Which plush will you be?","Draw mine and check our match","Check with the plush I already drew","You'll use the same mode as your inviting friend.","Connect our red thread","Send a red thread to a friend","Compatibility","About this match","A personal compatibility score needs two results drawn in the same mode.","{score} points","Where you fit together","Where you might bump heads","Care instructions for the two of us","Twin plushies","Connect with another friend","Stitched for each other","A perfect little knot","Strong, steady stitches","Stronger with a little mending","Let's untangle the thread","Secure","Anxious","Avoidant","Fearful-avoidant","Secret","Bestseller","Fan favorite","Rare","Secret","Share","Save image","Share image","Copy link","Copy compatibility link","Link copied. Pop it into your group chat!","Please copy the link below","Your nickname is included in the shared link","I drew an attachment plush: {type}","{nick} \xb7 Which attachment plush are you?","Hangtag card","Receipt","Care label","Compatibility card","Two-sides card","Story","Feed","Putting your precious plush on a card\u2026","Image saved","Couldn't save. Try sharing the image or saving it in your browser.","Can't save? Press and hold the image, or open this in an external browser.","Post to Instagram Stories","1. Save the image\n2. Open Instagram\n3. Choose the saved image in Stories","Attachment plush receipt","Guest","Mode","Coins used","16 coins","Plush drawn","Rarity","Payment method","One heart","No exchanges or refunds (attachment can change)","Two sides of my heart","In love","With friends","Draw in both modes to unlock your two-sides card.","My plush room","Today's little thought","My latest plush","Friends map","No red threads connected yet","Send a friend an invitation and fill in the map of your hearts.","Make a wallpaper","Dress up your lock screen with your plush and the color of your heart.","Settings","Language","Changing language keeps your progress and results.","Use device language","Language preference saved","Couldn't load that language. Your current language stays selected.","Reduce motion","Less swaying and shorter reveal animations.","Reset device records","Reset your records?","This removes your results, friends, collection and unfinished answers from this device.","Reset everything","Cancel","Close","OK","Open","Home","Back","Try again","Next","Done","About the test","Attachment styles and little plushies","Four levels on each of two axes make 16 plushies. At certain central scores, you'll meet the secret teddy bear.","Love and friendship modes use different situations but the same scoring rules. Attachment can change with relationship experiences.","No login; records stay on this device. Shared links contain scores, mode, scoring version and your optional nickname. These links are not encrypted secrets.","Support in South Korea: youth counseling 1388 \xb7 suicide prevention counseling 109. Elsewhere, check your local counseling or emergency support services.","A self-discovery test just for fun, not a medical or psychological diagnosis. Attachment can change with relationship experiences.","Privacy information","Where do my heart's records live?","Answers, results, your collection, friends and language preference are stored on this device. There is no server account or cross-device syncing. Resetting removes this device's test records, but cannot revoke links already shared. No external analytics or advertising services are connected in this app. Sharing an image or link to another app is subject to that service's policies.","Using this app","This is an entertainment test for self-understanding, not a substitute for professional counseling or diagnosis. Results can change with relationship experiences, and appearance rates are estimates. Shared links are neither certificates nor a way to identify a person. Final operating policies and contact details will be confirmed before release.","App version","Device storage is unavailable, so this session is temporary. Closing the window may lose your records.","Some saved records couldn't be read. You can still start a new test normally.","Oops, a plush escaped!","Couldn't load the content. Please try again.","Couldn't complete that action. Please try again.","Check this link","Couldn't read this shared link. Please check that the link is correct.","This scoring version isn't supported. Please update the app.","Please connect plushies drawn in the same mode.","Please answer all 16 questions.","Another test is in progress. Continue it, or clear its answers to start from this invitation.","Continue the existing test","Clear old answers and accept invitation","Paste a friend's link","Open a shared or compatibility link","What are you up to?","Still unread","2:13 PM","Yep","Can we talk about how we feel?","Can we have a heart-to-heart?","Loves me\u2026 loves me not\u2026","Canceled","{name} plush \u2014 {nick}","Your attachment style, as a plush","16 questions to meet a plush keychain shaped like your heart.","A red thread connects friends, too","Explore the knot between you and fill a lovable little collection.","A little attachment plush,\nhanging close to my heart","Take the test, connect with friends and keep a plush of your own.","Draw one on the web","App store release is being prepared","Aechak Plush \xb7 H1Soft","Contact us","Open-source licenses","Background pattern","Show quote","Solid","Dots","Grid","Stitches","Took a screenshot? Save a high-quality card instead?","Your KakaoTalk message to that person has stayed unread for three hours.","Your KakaoTalk message to your best friend has stayed unread for three hours.","Must be busy. Phone down, back to my own stuff.","I check now and then when it crosses my mind.","I reread what I sent. Did I say something wrong\u2026?","I've already finished three imaginary stories about us drifting apart.","On a night walk, they say, \u2018Can we talk about how we've been feeling lately?\u2019","Late at night, your best friend says, \u2018Can we have a serious heart-to-heart?\u2019","Yes! I've got plenty to say, too.","A bit shy, but I give talking a try.","I want to joke, \u2018Whoa, where did that come from?\u2019 and brush it off.","I want to escape. I already feel suffocated.","They usually flood you with stickers, but today the reply is just \u2018yep.\u2019","Your usually super-expressive best friend replies with only \u2018yep\u2019 today.","Probably tired. I'll ask if they're okay later.","It bothers me a little, then I forget about it.","I scroll back through our chat. Did I do something wrong?","I'm sure they've lost interest and feel hurt all on my own.","They say, \u2018Let's call every night before bed!\u2019","Your best friend says, \u2018Let's share our day every night before bed!\u2019","Love it. It feels like a lovely way to end the day.","Sounds nice, though I'd want a break sometimes.","Every day feels like a lot. I'm already thinking of excuses.","Even imagining it is tiring. Where did my own time go?","Their story shows them having a great time with people you don't know.","Your best friend's story shows them hanging out with other friends\u2014without you.","Looks fun! I tap the heart and move on.","Who are they? Briefly curious, then I move on.","They look happier than when they're with me, so I start comparing.","So they're fine without me\u2026 I feel down for the whole day.","You're sick in bed all day. They ask, \u2018Do you need anything?\u2019","You're sick in bed all day. Your best friend asks, \u2018Shall I bring you some porridge?\u2019","\u2018Yes, please come!\u2019 I honestly ask for help.","I feel bad and decline once, but eventually ask.","\u2018I'm fine, really!\u2019 I handle it on my own.","I didn't even tell them. I don't want to show I'm unwell.","After an argument, they say, \u2018I need some time to think.\u2019","After a little disagreement, your best friend says, \u2018I'll sort my thoughts out and get back to you.\u2019","Okay, let's talk when you're ready. I'll do my own things while I wait.","I'm a little anxious, but I wait for them to reach out.","I can't keep waiting, so I send, \u2018Are you still upset?\u2019","I keep writing and deleting a long message, scared this could be the end.","Saying \u2018I like you\u2019 to that person feels\u2026","Saying \u2018You really matter to me\u2019 to your best friend feels\u2026","Natural. If I think it, I say it.","A little embarrassing sometimes, but I say what I need to.","I feel it but can't get the words out. I show it through actions.","So awkward I practically can't do it.","How often do you want reassurance about how much they like you?","How often do you want reassurance about how much your best friend cares?","Hardly ever. I can feel it without checking.","Sometimes, but a few words are enough.","Often. I need to ask directly and hear the answer to relax.","Even after an answer, I'm anxious. I analyze their tone all over again.","Whenever things get hard, they lean on you for support.","Whenever things get hard, your best friend tells you first.","I like feeling that they trust me.","I like it, but sometimes it's a lot to carry.","I feel responsible and want to step back a little.","Having someone rely on me feels especially overwhelming.","They cancel a date you've been looking forward to the day before, saying something urgent came up.","Your best friend cancels plans you've been looking forward to the day before, saying something urgent came up.","Disappointing, but we can meet another day! I suggest a new date.","A little disappointed, but I understand.","Is it really urgent\u2026 or do they just not feel like seeing me?","So I'm not a priority after all. My hurt feelings are about to spill over.","They ask, \u2018What do you think we'll be doing a year from now?\u2019 and start talking about the distant future.","Your best friend says, \u2018Let's live together someday! And travel every year!\u2019","I get excited and make plans with them.","It's nice, but far away, so I just smile and listen.","It feels like promising the future, so I start backing away a little.","It weighs on me. I change the subject right away.","If you showed them every part of the real you\u2026","If you showed your best friend every part of the real you\u2026","I think they'd like me just as much as now.","Things might change a little, but I think it'd be okay.","I only show my better sides, worried I'd disappoint them.","Just imagining it scares me. I think they'd eventually leave.","You're spending the whole weekend together. By the second evening, you\u2026","You're on a three-day trip with your best friend. By the second evening, you\u2026","Still love it. Being together feels comfortable.","Am a little tired, but having fun.","Desperately need alone time. I pretend to go to the store and take a walk.","Am completely drained. I just want to go home and be alone.","They've really gotten into a new hobby lately and spend less time with you.","Your best friend has become close with new friends lately and spends less time with you.","Good for them for finding something fun! I enjoy my own time, too.","It feels a little empty, but I soon adjust.","Do they like that more than me\u2026? My hurt starts showing.","I feel like I'm being forgotten, so I contact them more often.","They ask, \u2018Is something worrying you lately?\u2019 There actually is something.","Your best friend asks, \u2018Something's been going on, hasn't it?\u2019 There actually is something.","I open up as if I've been waiting for them to ask.","I hesitate a little, then tell them.","\u2018No, nothing much!\u2019 I keep it to myself.","Talking about worries itself feels uncomfortable, so I change the subject.","Secure Puppy","A tail that wags with trust","A late reply is fine. We're still us!","I missed you! Just saying~","I'll use words, not my tail, when I'm hurt.","#EasygoingReplies","#TalkItOut","#TogetherOrAlone","Trusting close people comes naturally to this plush. If messages slow down, it thinks \u2018They must be busy,\u2019 and talks through hurt feelings instead of storing them up. Somehow, being around this person helps your heart relax.","A bad mood doesn't become an attitude","Says thank you and sorry right away","Puzzled by unexplained distance","Tired when always doing the adapting","Wash often with everyday kindness","Gently rinse out hurt feelings each day","A sunny walk leaves me fluffy","No games that test my trust","One conversation smooths out misunderstandings","Secure hearts can get tired, too. Don't always be the understanding one; try saying what you need first.","A steady wag is the best reassurance for a worried bunny","When the waiting drags on, even this tail droops","Secure Penguin","A sweetheart with a pebble for you","I picked this up thinking of you. It's nothing, hehe.","Winter isn't cold when we're huddled together.","How was your day? Tell me every little bit!","#TinyGiftExpert","#FullOfAffection","#LovesToHuddle","This plush shows affection often through little actions. It's happiest huddling close to someone it likes, and reaches out first even after a disagreement. When affection grows quieter, though, it has a cute tendency to look a little gloomy.","Remembers and cares for the little details","Knows how to reach out first after a fight","When its affection gets no response","When only it remembers a special day","Wash often with warm reactions","Fluff dry with a hug","Don't forget a gift you received","Give thanks one extra rinse in words","Smooth hurt feelings with a lukewarm talk","Practice receiving as well as giving. Saying \u2018I need this, too\u2019 isn't a burden\u2014it's another kind of gift.","An affectionate penguin and a relaxed capybara have just the right temperature difference","The closer the penguin comes, the further the turtle retreats","Secure Capybara","Calm with a tangerine on top","Together is nice. Apart is nice, too. Peace~","No rush. Let's take our time.","Angry? Nope, just thinking about hot springs.","#PeaceItself","#TogetherAndIndependent","#HotSpringMind","This plush has room to breathe in relationships. Time together and time alone are equally precious, and most things don't shake it. It gets along comfortably with almost anyone, so people gather around it naturally.","Steady without big emotional swings","Respects the other person's own time","Being told it's hard to read","Being repeatedly pushed to express feelings","Wash at a lukewarm hot-spring temperature","Shade dry during alone time","No hurry-up tumble drying","Sometimes rinse with an \u2018I like you\u2019 first","Gently smooth hurt hidden under calmness","Your calm can sometimes look like indifference. Even when everything is fine, let them know with an occasional \u2018I'm happy right now.\u2019","The capybara's back is the duckling's favorite spot","The tiger may read a calm face as not caring","Secure Otter","Holding hands even in sleep","I'll hold your hand so we don't drift away.","I need time to open clams alone, too. Back soon!","We're okay, right? Yes, I know we are.","#HandsHeldTight","#BalanceExpert","#HappyAloneToo","This plush balances closeness and independence well. It enjoys playing alone but wants to hold hands when falling asleep. Sometimes it needs reassurance, yet it's also quite good at soothing its own heart.","Finds a comfortable amount of space","Honestly leans on others when needed","When contact patterns suddenly change","When alone time hurts someone's feelings","Light daily wash with a hello","Air dry during your separate time","No letting go and drifting away","Gently rinse anxiety with hand-holding","Smooth small misunderstandings that day","You're good at comforting yourself. Trust that strength, but don't swallow everything alone. Sometimes ask, \u2018Could you hold my hand?\u2019","It gently takes the hand of a cat pretending to be cool","An otter is startled when the pufferfish puffs up as it reaches out","Anxious Duckling","Following you everywhere","Where are you going? I'll come! I just\u2026 want to be together.","From the moment we met, I decided to follow only you.","I didn't count the minutes until your reply. Really.","#AlwaysFollowing","#AffectionMaxed","#RepliesComeFirst","This plush follows the person it cares about everywhere. It can't hide its affection, so it usually reaches out and expresses feelings first. That also means even a slightly cooler response quickly weighs on its heart, leaving it wanting reassurance.","Gives affection without holding back","Notices even small changes in others","Feeling like it's the only one who cares more","Replies taking longer than usual","Please rinse with a reply within 20 minutes","Wash with an \u2018I missed you, too\u2019","No suddenly cold-attitude drying","A reassurance net is essential in new places","Listen to my whole story for a fluffy finish","The more you follow someone, the smaller your own steps can become. Today, put one thing you like first\u2014not just what they like.","The capybara's back is the duckling's comfiest place","The duckling gets lost during the panda's bamboo time","Anxious Bunny","Please don't leave me lonely","If you've read it, reply\u2026 No, it's fine\u2026 No, it isn't.","If you're fine without me\u2026 that hurts in its own way.","Say you like me. Again. Actually, three times.","#ReassuranceAgain","#LonelinessSensitive","#LoveOvercharged","Love is this plush's energy. Its heart is big and deep, so silence or even a slight change of tone can send it spinning. Asking \u2018Do you like me?\u2019 again and again isn't suspicion; each answer helps it feel safe.","Loves with its whole heart","Especially sensitive to others' feelings","A long wait with an unread message","Vague distance without an explanation","Reply within 10 minutes; short is okay","Rinse with \u2018I like you\u2019 three times daily","Absolutely no disappearing in the dryer","Set a reassurance net before stepping away","Smooth an anxious night with your voice","When anxiety rises, soothe yourself for ten minutes before sending a reassurance message. A favorite song, a warm drink. Your worthiness of love isn't measured by reply speed.","With that steady wag nearby, the bunny's ears can relax","The more the bunny calls, the farther the owl flies","Anxious Cat","Cool outside, checking every minute","Replies? Don't care. (Just refreshed seven times.)","Texting first means losing. \u2026But I miss you.","Am I okay? Yep. Not okay, but okay.","#PretendingToBeCool","#RefreshingInside","#CantTextFirst","This plush looks proud and cool on the outside, but watches replies and expressions more closely than anyone. It tends to replay hurt feelings alone instead of showing them, so even people nearby may not know what's in its heart.","Reads others' moods uncannily well","Quietly affectionate with people it likes","When it feels like it should reach out first","A short reply after a long wait","Reply within 30 minutes; add a sticker","No wringing with \u2018What's wrong?\u2019","Rinse with an \u2018I missed you\u2019 first","Wait a little in the shade when I'm sulking","Smooth out the sincerity beneath my prickly tone","Acting cool protects your heart, but can keep others from getting to know you. One sentence\u2014\u2018That hurt me a little\u2019\u2014is enough to share a feeling.","The otter holds hands with the anxiety hiding behind the cool act","The sloth's relaxed replies keep the cat refreshing inside","Anxious Tiger","Growling when worried","Roar! \u2026I'm scared, actually. Don't leave me behind.","I'm not angry! I am! No, I was hurt\u2026","If you don't text first, neither will I. (I want to.)","#ToughOutsideSoftInside","#GrowlIsSOS","#HurtFeelingsOverflow","This plush acts tougher when anxiety grows. When hurt, \u2018Roar!\u2019 comes out before \u2018I'm okay,\u2019 which can cause misunderstandings. But that growl is really a rescue signal saying, \u2018Please notice me.\u2019","Takes relationships deeply to heart","Extra affectionate after making up","When a conversation ends without an answer","Feeling pushed down the priority list","Soothe my growls within 10 minutes","No bleaching with \u2018What now?\u2019","Gently rinse the truth behind tough words","No disappearing before we've made up","Iron out a reunion with a warm hug","Before a growl, pause for just three seconds and name it: \u2018I'm anxious right now.\u2019 Sharing anxiety instead of anger helps the other person see your heart, not your claws.","The penguin sees the tears behind the roar and offers a pebble","The more the tiger growls, the deeper the turtle hides","Avoidant Panda","Bamboo time is alone time","I like you. But right now, I'd like to eat bamboo alone.","I'm not ignoring you because I dislike you. I'm recharging.","They say pandas live alone in the wild. Really.","#AloneToRecharge","#MyTimeMatters","#OccasionalMessages","This plush likes people, but needs alone time to smile again. Wild pandas actually tend to live alone, too. Less contact doesn't mean its feelings have cooled; after recharging, it comes back with affection.","Respects each other's time","Gives full attention when together","Being expected to report in all day","When wanting alone time hurts the other person","Shade drying is essential for bamboo time","No drying with \u2018Why aren't you texting?\u2019","Keep contact lukewarm but steady","Hang up plans ahead of time for comfort","Praise the messages I send first","Before disappearing for alone time, just say, \u2018I'm going to recharge; I'll be back!\u2019 That one sentence can be a huge reassurance.","Doing your own things, but holding hands at bedtime","Being followed everywhere leaves no bamboo time","Avoidant Owl","Most comfortable on my own","I'm okay on my own. \u2026I really am, mostly.","Feelings talk? Tomorrow-me can handle that.","I'm not uninterested. I'm quietly watching from afar.","#IndependenceMaxed","#PrivateFeelings","#WatchingFromAfar","This plush is most comfortable handling everything itself. Leaning on someone\u2014or having someone lean on it\u2014can feel a little heavy. It may seem cold, but its way of caring is to quietly watch over people from a distance.","Calm and dependable in a crisis","Doesn't try to control the other person","A sudden wish for a deep emotional talk","Being asked to define \u2018What are we?\u2019","Nighttime drying alone is essential","No wringing out my inner thoughts","Don't rush-dry the relationship","Wash feelings talks in 20-minute portions","Keep praise simple and low-temperature","Being okay alone is a lovely strength. Still, try asking someone close, \u2018Could you help me with this?\u2019 Leaning on others gets easier with practice.","With an unhurried capybara, the owl comes out even by day","The bunny's calls send it to an even farther branch","Avoidant Sloth","Letting you in, slowly","Sorry I replied late\u2026 I spent three hours thinking about it.","Opening up takes me a while. But I stay for a long time.","Let's\u2026 get\u2026 close\u2026 slowly\u2026","#SlowReplies","#SincereHeart","#SlowStarter","This plush needs time to open its heart. Slow replies and expressions can be misunderstood, but once it opens up, it hangs on for a long time. Being pushed to move quickly only makes it pull farther away.","Stays close for a long time once bonded","Consistent in actions more than words","Being pushed to reply quickly","When a relationship moves too fast","Please dry slowly on low heat","No hurry-up tumble drying","Gently read the sincerity in a slow reply","Hang me on a familiar routine","Smooth hurt before it piles up","Being slow isn't wrong. When a reply will take time, saying \u2018I'm thinking; I'll reply properly later\u2019 can make the wait much easier for someone else.","The otter doesn't let go, even when things move slowly","A relaxed reply is endless refresh-button time for the cat","Avoidant Turtle","Big feelings? Into my shell","Just a moment\u2026 I'll think inside my shell and come back.","I hid because I didn't want to fight, not because I dislike you.","You'll be the first person I go to when I come out.","#IntoTheShell","#AvoidsConflict","#GentleWhenReady","When feelings become a lot, this plush retreats into its shell. Going quiet during a fight or serious talk isn't dislike; its heart is simply too noisy. When it feels safe, it slowly peeks out again.","Doesn't anger or hurt others easily","Speaks honestly after sorting things out","A conversation with raised voices","Being told to decide right this second","Put on a safety net before an argument","Don't force my shell open","A day in the shade helps me come out","Rinse with gentle words when I emerge","No drying with \u2018Talk right now\u2019","Before hiding, promise a time to return: \u2018I need time to sort this out. Let's talk tomorrow.\u2019 Disappearing and taking an agreed break are different.","The puppy waits, tail wagging, until the turtle comes out","A growl makes the shell door slam shut","Fearful Mole","Popping out, then hiding again","I miss you! \u2026Actually, I think I'll hide today.","Come closer and I want to hide. Move away and I want to hold on.","It's not whack-a-mole\u2026 that's just my heart.","#NotPlayingGames","#OutThenIn","#WhackAMoleHeart","Wanting closeness and wanting to hide from hurt take turns peeking out in this plush. It may reach out yesterday and go quiet today, which can look like playing games. Really, its heart is running in two directions at once.","Connects deeply when sincerity gets through","Empathizes with others' anxiety","A relationship suddenly becoming close","Or feeling it growing distant","Wash steadily at the same temperature","No toy hammer when I'm hiding","Wait by the burrow on hiding days","Rinse with \u2018Good to see you\u2019 when I emerge","Slowly smooth my up-and-down feelings","When your heart goes back and forth, narrate it instead of acting it out. \u2018I want to be close, but I'm a little scared\u2019 helps the other person know how to wait.","A steady pebble offered every time it comes back out","If both are wobbling, who will hold on?","Fearful Hedgehog","Wanting hugs, raising spines","Hug me. Oh, don't come close. No, hug me\u2026","My spines are up because I'm scared, not to prick you.","The hedgehog's dilemma? That's literally my story.","#HedgehogDilemma","#DefensiveSpines","#SoftInside","This plush wants love deeply, but as someone comes closer, fear of getting hurt raises its spines first. Sharp words sometimes slip out, followed by regret. Underneath is a soft little belly; when it feels safe, the spines slowly settle.","Understands the weight of hurt","Stays by you once it learns to trust","Sudden closeness without warning","Feeling criticized for a small mistake","Hand-wash gently with the spines","No bleaching away old wounds","Approach slowly, at low heat","Use a reassuring tone, not loud voices","On spiky days, quietly stay nearby","Noticing when your spines rise is already half the work. Say to yourself, \u2018I think I'm defending myself right now.\u2019 When it's too much, share it with someone you trust.","The puppy's tail keeps wagging even when the spines rise","Spines and claws go up at the same time","Fearful Pufferfish","Puffing up when hurt","I'm not upset. (Puff.) Really, I'm not. (Puff puff puff.)","Puffing up is how I protect myself.","I'll speak first once the air is out. Give me a little time.","#PuffedUpDefense","#PretendingImFine","#DeflatingNow","This plush puffs up to protect itself when its heart gets hurt. In a painful moment, it says \u2018I'm fine\u2019 and pulls away, while secretly hoping someone will notice first. Only after the air settles does it bring out its real feelings.","Has strength to get through things alone","Especially honest once it opens up","A prickly comment disguised as a joke","Someone deciding how it feels for it","Quiet deflating time when puffed up","No pressing me flat by force","Check \u2018Are you okay?\u2019 again in 30 minutes","No bleaching with \u2018You're too sensitive\u2019","Gently hug me once the air is out","When \u2018I'm fine\u2019 becomes a habit, real okay moments can get lost. As you start to puff up, try a short sentence: \u2018That hurt me a little.\u2019","Even when it puffs up, the capybara simply stays nearby","The more the bunny checks, the more the pufferfish puffs","Fearful Jellyfish","A heart riding the waves","Come closer\u2026 But too close, and I might give a little sting.","Swaying wherever the waves take me.","You think I'm see-through? Even I don't know my own heart.","#EmotionalWaves","#TransparentSincerity","#TinyStingWarning","The wish to be loved and the wish not to get hurt wash over this plush in alternating waves. Moving closer and farther away can tire it out, too. Yet it has a sparkling heart that senses people with extraordinary delicacy.","Reads emotions with great sensitivity","Shines wholeheartedly once it trusts","Unpredictable attitudes from others","A small sign that someone might leave","A steady-temperature safety net is essential","Tentacles are hand-wash only, gently","No sudden changes in attitude","Rest in calm water on stingy days","Professional care is okay when the heart feels heavy","Your heart's waves are sensitivity, not weakness. Choose an anchor for shaky moments\u2014a walk, a journal or someone you trust. Asking a professional for help when it's too much is brave, too.","The otter holds its hand so it won't drift away","Two hearts riding waves means double the seasickness","Secret Teddy Bear","The original attachment plush","I know your heart. I've got a little of every part, too.","Congrats on the secret! A photo is a must.","My shape changes a little with each person I meet.","#Secret","#OriginalComfortPlush","#UltimateBalance","Anxiety and avoidance sit right in the middle for this plush, with a little of all four hearts inside. That's why it changes shape depending on whom it meets and can understand every plush's heart. The teddy bear, where all attachment plushies began, chose you.","Can connect with any type","Adapts flexibly to the situation","Losing itself while adapting to everyone","Not knowing its own heart either","Wash at body temperature: 36.5\xb0","Mend the places worn by fitting in","Sometimes hang somewhere just for me","No bleaching out my own colors","I'm a rare item; store with care","A balanced heart is a strength, but changing shape for every relationship can make you forget the real you. Write down the moment today when you felt most at ease.","The original comfort plush meets the original good dog","No plush to watch out for. Just you, worn out from adapting to everyone!","A sunny windowsill","Both hearts feel at ease, so time passes gently when you're together.","You share joy and hurt in words each day","Forgetting to make room for sparks because you're so comfortable","Freshen things up with something new now and then","Don't let familiarity replace gratitude","Create little anniversaries just for you two","A cozy blanket","A secure heart's steadiness wraps an anxious heart in warmth.","The comfort of reassurance when anxiety rises","When the secure one brushes it off as \u2018It's nothing\u2019","Offer a little explanation when anxiety shows","Say \u2018I see\u2019 instead of \u2018It's nothing\u2019","The anxious one can express thanks right away, too","Closeness, little by little","When a secure heart waits without rushing, an avoidant heart slowly opens up.","Comfort in respecting each other's space","When one person's closeness feels heavy to the other","Share plans for alone time in advance","The avoidant one promises when they'll return","Notice even the smallest expressions of affection","A lighthouse and a little boat","For a wavering fearful heart, a secure heart is a lighthouse in the same place.","The safety of a steady point even in waves","When the secure one grows tired of shifting feelings","Stay consistent in words and warmth","The fearful one narrates their feelings","The secure one takes time to rest, too","A call at two in the morning","You know each other's worries so well that your connection runs deep and warm.","Plentiful affection and quick empathy","When both become anxious, worries double","Take turns being the reassuring one","Keep reassurance questions to once a day","Each build a calming routine of your own","Roommates with separate rooms","Respect for each other's space feels comfortable, but closeness grows slowly.","Freedom without interference","When both put off important conversations","Have a heart-to-heart once a month","Agree on contact expectations in advance","Shower the one who reaches out first with praise","Attachment hide-and-seek","As one moves closer, the other moves away\u2014the famous attachment chase.","You're drawn to what the other has and you don't","Chasing creates running, and running creates more chasing","Avoidant: say when you'll return before stepping away","Anxious: soothe yourself for ten minutes before chasing","Both: talk through your contact expectations","Side by side on a roller coaster","You ride emotional ups and downs together. Thrilling, but sometimes dizzying.","Deep understanding of each other's anxiety","When one hides, the other gets more anxious","Leave a sentence explaining why you need to hide","Turn anxiety into a request, not blame","Agree on one promise that feels like a seat belt","A walk in the fog","You both sometimes step back, so your hearts can easily disappear into the fog.","Understanding each other's need for distance","When both stay silent and misunderstandings pile up","Send a signal first if silence stretches on","Ask instead of guessing","Check in daily, even briefly","Riding the waves","You understand each other deeply, but the waves grow when both hearts shake.","Deep empathy that needs few words","When you both hide or both wobble at once","Use an \u2018I'm riding a wave\u2019 signal","When one wobbles, the other becomes an anchor","Reach out for outside support together when needed","A soft bundle of fluff","Teddy's flexibility and a secure heart's ease make things twice as cozy.","Gently finding a way to fit together","When both keep yielding and decisions take forever","Sometimes be the first to choose and decide","Make a little spark inside the comfort","Say thank you twice, out loud","A warm-hearted translator","Teddy notices an anxious heart as if translating it, then gives it a hug.","Quickly spotting signals of anxiety","When Teddy gets tired from always adapting","The anxious one shows gratitude","Teddy shares hurt feelings, too","Create a reassuring routine together","An unhurried translator","Teddy respects an avoidant heart's space while quietly staying nearby.","Balancing distance and closeness well","When only Teddy keeps reaching out first","The avoidant one reaches out first sometimes, too","Give a heads-up before alone time","Praise even little expressions of affection","A calm little harbor","For a fearful heart riding waves, Teddy can be a calm harbor.","Understanding a heart that changes direction","When Teddy starts wobbling along, too","Narrate the wobble in words","Teddy needs days off, too","Keep promises small and steady","The legendary teddy duo","Two one-percent secrets have met. That's practically a legend.","Understanding each other like a mirror","When both adapt and neither makes a decision","A photo is a must","Take turns choosing","Ask about each other's real preferences"],t.w)
